{
  "id": "semantic_roles",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "depends_on": [
    "situation_model"
  ],
  "description": "Semantic-role extraction (who-did-what-to-whom): a structural pass assigns provisional roles from POSITION + PREPOSITION + VOICE (robust), then a verb-FRAME pass refines where those under-determine (to->recipient/goal, with->instrument, unaccusative subject->theme). assign_role is one graph rule over argument nodes; the parse (tokenise, find verb, group NPs, tag PPs/voice) is mechanical. Output = the role-tuples the situation model eats: raw text -> roles -> situation model.",
  "microtheory": {
    "name": "semantic_roles",
    "description": "predicate-argument role labelling"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "local_id": 1,
      "type": "Concept",
      "attrs": {
        "name": "semantic_role",
        "description": "The thematic role an argument plays in a predicate: agent (doer), theme/patient (undergoer), recipient, goal, instrument, source, location. Extracted as typed ROLE edges from a predicate node to its argument NPs \u2014 the same tuple the situation model eats."
      }
    },
    {
      "local_id": 2,
      "type": "Concept",
      "attrs": {
        "name": "predicate_frame",
        "description": "A small per-verb-lemma fragment listing which roles the verb licenses and how each surface slot binds: it refines the structural guess where position+preposition under-determine (to -> recipient for a transfer verb give/send vs goal for a motion verb walk/go; with -> instrument for cut vs accompaniment for dance; an unaccusative verb shatter/break/melt makes its SUBJECT the theme, not the agent). Unknown verb -> keep the structural guess (graceful)."
      }
    },
    {
      "local_id": 3,
      "type": "Principle",
      "attrs": {
        "name": "roles_structural_first",
        "head": "semantic roles",
        "body": "the robust cues are structural and trusted without the verb: POSITION (NP before the verb = provisional agent, bare NP after = theme), PREPOSITION (each PP tagged by its function-word head to/with/from/in), and VOICE (be + past participle flips the subject to theme and the by-phrase carries the agent) \u2014 the same marker/adjacency machinery as the simile and perspective tests"
      }
    },
    {
      "local_id": 4,
      "type": "Principle",
      "attrs": {
        "name": "roles_frame_refines",
        "head": "semantic roles",
        "body": "the verb FRAME overrides the provisional label only where it is more specific (to->recipient vs goal, with->instrument vs accompaniment, unaccusative subject->theme), leaving the structural guess in place for unknown verbs \u2014 graceful degradation, never a crash"
      }
    },
    {
      "local_id": 5,
      "type": "Principle",
      "attrs": {
        "name": "roles_feed_situation_model",
        "head": "semantic roles",
        "body": "the output is the clean tuple the situation model consumes: one predicate with fully-labelled role edges, voice resolved (the agent is the agent regardless of surface order) and prepositions resolved to thematic roles rather than left as raw to/with"
      }
    }
  ],
  "edges": [],
  "rules": [
